{"uid":"55d250be159b8d71","name":"test_prompt_lookup_deadline_exceeds_mlflow_http_timeout","fullName":"tests.test_routes_prompts#test_prompt_lookup_deadline_exceeds_mlflow_http_timeout","historyId":"59d8103de4e86f3f2cf30c9db7e7e8db","time":{"start":1789819272087,"stop":1789819272089,"duration":2},"description":"``_PROMPT_LOOKUP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`` must stay above the MLflow HTTP\n    client's own timeout, or every merely-*slow* (not hung) registry call is\n    guaranteed to be aborted by our deadline before it can succeed or fail on\n    its own -- which just turns it into an orphaned thread that keeps\n    occupying a ``_prompt_lookup_executor`` worker for however much longer\n    MLflow's timeout takes. Repeated page loads during any MLflow slowdown\n    then progressively starve the fixed-size pool. Read straight from\n    server.py's default rather than hardcoding \"15\" a second time here, so\n    this test still catches drift if that default ever changes.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>_PROMPT_LOOKUP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS</code> must stay above the MLflow HTTP<br />\nclient's own timeout, or every merely-<em>slow</em> (not hung) registry call is<br />\nguaranteed to be aborted by our deadline before it can succeed or fail on<br />\nits own -- which just turns it into an orphaned thread that keeps<br />\noccupying a <code>_prompt_lookup_executor</code> worker for however much longer<br />\nMLflow's timeout takes. Repeated page loads during any MLflow slowdown<br />\nthen progressively starve the fixed-size pool. Read straight from<br />\nserver.py's default rather than hardcoding &quot;15&quot; a second time here, so<br />\nthis test still catches drift if that default ever changes.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1789818303305,"stop":1789818303305,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachment